		"Suspiria": {
			"title": "Suspiria",
			"description": "1977 Italian horror film by Dario Argento",
			"extract": "Suspiria is a 1977 Italian supernatural horror film directed by Dario Argento, who co-wrote the screenplay with Daria Nicolodi, partially based on Thomas De Quincey's 1845 essay Suspiria de Profundis. The film stars Jessica Harper as an American ballet student who transfers to a prestigious European dance academy but realizes, after a series of murders, that the school is a front for something sinister. It also features Stefania Casini, Flavio Bucci, Miguel Bos\u00e9, Alida Valli, Udo Kier, and Joan Bennett, in her final film role.",
			"extract_html": "<p><i><b>Suspiria</b></i> is a 1977 Italian supernatural horror film directed by Dario Argento, who co-wrote the screenplay with Daria Nicolodi, partially based on Thomas De Quincey's 1845 essay <i>Suspiria de Profundis</i>. The film stars Jessica Harper as an American ballet student who transfers to a prestigious European dance academy but realizes, after a series of murders, that the school is a front for something sinister. It also features Stefania Casini, Flavio Bucci, Miguel Bos\u00e9, Alida Valli, Udo Kier, and Joan Bennett, in her final film role.</p>",
